{"url": "https://www.uu.nl/en/education/phd-at-the-graduate-school-of-life-sciences/starting-your-phd/prospective-phd-candidates", "final_url": "https://www.uu.nl/en/education/phd-at-the-graduate-school-of-life-sciences/starting-your-phd/prospective-phd-candidates", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-26", "text": "Prospective PhD candidates | Utrecht University\nSkip to main content Menu\nSearch uu.nl\nSearch scope\nSubject\nStaff member\nSearch\nSelect language\nNederlands nl\nBreadcrumb\nHome\nEducation\nPhD at the Graduate School of Life Sciences\nStarting your PhD\nProspective PhD candidates\nPhD at the Graduate School of Life Sciences\nPhD at the Graduate School of Life Sciences\nPhD at the Graduate School of Life Sciences\nStarting your PhD Close submenu +\nProspective PhD candidates\nGetting started Close submenu +\nResponsibilities of PhD candidates\nCategories of PhD candidates\nSupervision\nMyPhD\nTraining and Supervision Agreement (TSA)\nDuring your PhD Close submenu +\nPhD training Close submenu +\nPhD Competence Model\nCompulsory training\nPhD Course Centre Close submenu +\nCourse Descriptions Close submenu +\nResearch Skills and Knowledge\nResponsible Conduct of Science\nCommunication\nTeaching\nLeadership and Management\nPersonal Effectiveness\nProfessional Development\nAll Courses\nCourse Schedule\nPhD Update\nIntroduction Meeting\nInterviews with Trainers\nPhD programmes\nTracking your progress\nSupport during your PhD\nEvents Close submenu +\nPhD Day Close submenu +\n2026 - Under Pressure\n2025 - Mind Your Gap\n2024 - Scientists of the Future\nSupervisor of the Year Award Close submenu +\n2025 - Supervisor of the Year\n2024 - Supervisor of the Year\n2023 - Supervisor of the Year\nLife Sciences PhD & Postdoc Career Week Close submenu +\n2026 - Life Sciences PhD & Postdoc Career Week\n2025 - Life Sciences PhD & Postdoc Career Week\nFinishing your PhD Close submenu +\nDoctoral thesis\nPreparation PhD defence\nGSLS Training Certificate\nLife after PhD\nPhD supervisors Close submenu +\nEffective supervisor \u2013 PhD interaction\nMonitoring your PhD candidate\nTraining in supervision Close submenu +\nSupervising PhD candidates at the GSLS\nMasterclass Responsible Conduct of Research for PhD Supervisors at UMC Utrecht\nSupervising PhD Candidates: Next Level\nPeer Consultation / Intervision\nProfessional Consult\nVideo Coaching\nMasterclasses offered by the PhD Psychologist\nDoctoral thesis\nAbout us Close submenu +\nPhD Team\nAnnual reviews\nPhD Councils Close submenu +\nPhD Survey\nPhD programme leaders and coordinators\nFAQs Close submenu +\nFAQs PhD track\nFAQs PhD Course Centre\nQuick links and downloads\nUU home\nPhD at the Graduate School of Life Sciences\nStarting your PhD\nProspective PhD candidates\nGetting started\nSupervision\nMyPhD\nTraining and Supervision Agreement (TSA)\nDuring your PhD\nFinishing your PhD\nLife after PhD\nPhD supervisors\nAbout us\nFAQs\nQuick links and downloads\nProspective PhD candidates\nThere are different options for obtaining a PhD position at Utrecht University. As a PhD candidate in the Netherlands, you are not a student but a university employee in most cases. If we are not able to employ you, you may want to look for funding in your country of residence for private scholarships.\nAt the GSLS, the PhD track is generally 4 years full-time, but must be at least 3 years full-time. This is determined by the Life Sciences Deans and applies to all PhD types. In case of part-time track, the duration is proportionally extended.\nPlease visit websites of the PhD programmes and Life Sciences institutes and research groups to find out if your research interest is available in Utrecht. The GSLS is not involved in recruiting and hiring PhD candidates. You must contact the researchers to discuss possibilities for a PhD position. Also have a look at the current vacancies of Utrecht University and vacancies of UMC Utrecht.\nRequirements you need to meet\nA master or equivalent degree is needed to be admitted to the PhD track. If you do not possess a Master (or equivalent) degree, you need to follow a different procedure (pdf).\nBefore you can start your PhD, you should have a supervisory team. Please visit websites of the PhD programmes and Life Sciences institutes and research groups to find out if your research interest is available in Utrecht. You can contact the researchers to discuss possibilities for a PhD position. Also have a look at the current vacancies of Utrecht University and vacancies of UMC Utrecht.\nPhD applicants have to demonstrate mastery of English before being accepted. The EMI-experienced level is required, with proof and exceptions as defined for UU Master students. Proof of proficiency must be provided to the selection committee before selection or acceptance.\u202fEnglish proficiency should also be assessed as sufficient for scientific discussions and daily informal conversation, by the selection committee during the selection/acceptance interview.\nMore information\nYou can find more information on how to obtain a PhD at Utrecht University at the PhD website of the university.\nObtaining a PhD position at Utrecht University\nFooter menu (EN)\nGo to\nChoose a programme\nStudent information\nJobs\nAlumni\nGiving\nServices\nIntranet for employees\nCourse planner\nMy Timetable\nAbout UU\nContact\nDirectory\nDisclaimer\nPrivacy\nContact\nFollow UU\nFacebook\nYoutube\nLinkedIn\nInstagram\nUtrecht University\nHeidelberglaan 8\n3584 CS Utrecht\nThe Netherlands\nTel. +31 (0)30 253 35 50", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.uu.nl/en/education/phd-at-the-graduate-school-of-life-sciences/starting-your-phd/prospective-phd-candidates#main-content"], ["", "https://www.uu.nl/en"], ["Nederlands nl", "https://www.uu.nl/"], ["Home", "https://www.uu.nl/en"], ["Education", "https://www.uu.nl/en/education"], ["PhD at the Graduate School of Life Sciences", "https://www.uu.nl/en/education/phd-at-the-graduate-school-o